<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $169.2 mln Feb 21.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $169.2 mln Feb 21.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $169.2 million surplus on February 21 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 21</p>
<p>Exports: $173.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $238.8 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $498.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $264 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $169.2 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.371 million</p>
<p>Imports: $2.304 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.587 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.507 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.147 billion ((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418))</p>
</text>
